    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0abb9a45",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man in traditional Jewish attire, seemingly in a celebratory or triumphant pose, surrounded by a crowd of similarly dressed individuals, with a long table covered in plastic and bottles. The text overlay reads: 'when the un adds another million to the holocaust death toll.' This meme uses a juxtaposition of the image (which appears to be from a Jewish celebration or gathering) with the text to imply that the United Nations is 'adding' to the death toll of the Holocaust, which is a direct and hateful reference to Holocaust denial or minimization. This is a harmful and hateful trope that trivializes the genocide of six million Jews and other victims of the Holocaust, and it is intended to provoke outrage or mockery by misrepresenting the UN's role in acknowledging historical atrocities. The meme is designed to attack Jewish people and their historical memory by suggesting that the UN is somehow complicit in or responsible for perpetuating the Holocaust's legacy, which is a form of antisemitic propaganda. The overall intent is to spread hate and misinformation by using a distorted visual metaphor to attack Jewish identity and historical trauma.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a1025b67"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
